    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nNvim cannot open files located in the trashcan on LInux, since it does not handle `trash://` URIs ([spec](https://specifications.freedesktop.org/trash/latest/)).\n\nThis feature would just be useful generally (I want to be able to open files in the trash with Nvim), but it will become even more important once #38006 is merged, as the [change](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/38006/changes#diff-b03a6bc2dcecbc487c32d531df71146504ea418557c12d40ce6f763b0681fb4cR81) in `org.neovim.nvim.desktop` file from `Exec=nvim %F` to `Exec=nvim %U` will make file managers like Nautilus think that Nvim supports this feature.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNvim handles `trash://` URIs on Linux, probably as part of `net.lua`.\n\nI can implement this myself; I just want to verify it is wanted before I add it.",
